course: dictionary
lesson: 1333
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. «About 540 million years ago, many animal groups with shells, eyes and legs appeared fairly quickly, in the Cambrian explosion.» The words around Cambrian are about animals and time, so it must be a period of Earth's history, not a place.
explain: «The Cambrian Mountains run through mid-Wales.» Now the clue is mountains and Wales, so Cambrian means to do with Wales. Always ask: what are the words around this word about? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Notice the capital letters and the little words around it. «The Cambrian» names a time, while «Cambrian» on its own can describe something, like Cambrian rocks. When you meet a familiar word in a new subject, check the context before you decide what it means.
fact: Cambrian is an adjective when it describes something, as in «the Cambrian Mountains».
fact: «The Cambrian» is a noun when it names a period of Earth's history, about 540 to 485 million years ago.
fact: In the Cambrian, many kinds of animals with hard shells first appeared in the sea.
fact: Cambrian means to do with Wales, from Cambria, the Latin name for Wales.
fact: A word can have different meanings in different subjects, so check the context.
exercise: «About 540 million years ago, many animal groups with shells, eyes and legs appeared fairly quickly, in the Cambrian explosion.» In this sentence, what does Cambrian mean? | A bird that lives in the sea | *A period of Earth's history, long ago | A town in the north of Wales | A mountain you can climb
exercise: «The Cambrian Mountains run through mid-Wales.» What does Cambrian mean here? | Very old, like a ruin | To do with the sea and animals | *To do with Wales | Made of hard shells
exercise: What does «appeared» mean in «many animal groups appeared fairly quickly»? | Disappeared | Painted | *Came into existence or showed up | Weighed
test: What is «the Cambrian» when it names a period of Earth's history? | A kind of railway in Wales | *A period of Earth's history about 540 to 485 million years ago | A period of time about 540 to 485 million years ago | A Welsh word meaning sea
test: Why is it helpful to ask what the words around a word are about? | They tell you how to spell the word | Cambrian never has more than one meaning | *They give clues to which meaning fits | They show that Cambrian is always a noun
exam: Which fact about the Cambrian is true? | It is a Welsh word meaning sea | *Many kinds of animals with hard shells first appeared in the sea | It means very old, like a ruin | Trilobites lived only on land
